  },
  "note": "Election of the Coleraine Borough Council, 20 May 1964: four aldermen and nine councillors returned unopposed, three councillor seats left unfilled (Londonderry Sentinel, 13 May 1964, p. 14). Only nine candidates were nominated for the twelve councillor seats, so there was no contest and three seats were left unfilled. All nine were outgoing members except S. W. Gordon and S. McFeely. No party label was printed. Returned unopposed."
